// The provider-agnostic vocabulary of the AI abstraction: the conversation history shape and a model
// step's outcome. Every element is a closed Katari type and never a wire token, so each provider maps it
// onto its own tokens by matching, and no one API's vocabulary becomes the abstraction's.

@"Whose turn this is: the caller's side of the conversation — a person's message, a system framing turn,
a background report, a turn the loop synthesized."
data user_role()

@"Whose turn this is: the model's own — text it produced on an earlier step and that is replayed to it as
its own words. The wire token differs per provider; which one goes out is the adapter's decision, made by
matching this sum."
data model_role()

// Who spoke one turn — a closed sum, so a provider adapter must map it and an app cannot invent a third
// value. (Type synonyms take no docs.)
type role = user_role | model_role

@"One turn in a conversation: who spoke, what they said, and any files attached to it. Files ride as blob
handles and each provider decides when to inline their content. @author@ is the optional opaque end-user
tag of a user turn (e.g. a hashed chat-user id), never shown to the model — a provider whose API has an
abuse-attribution field lifts the newest user turn's author into it (`ai.attribution`). `null` (the
default) means the turn is not attributable to an end user."
data turn(role: role, text: string, files: array[file] ?= [], author: string | null ?= null)

@"The correlation handle of one tool call: a single opaque token, minted by the provider that parsed the
model's pick and replayed verbatim on the call turn and on the result that answers it. What it holds is
the provider's own business, and nothing above the provider reads it: a result and its call correlate by
carrying the same value."
data call_ref(@"The provider's opaque per-call token, replayed verbatim." token: string)

@"One tool the model wants to invoke this step — @name@ is its function name (the dispatch key), @ref@ is
the call's opaque correlation handle, and @args@ is the model's argument object as a parsed value,
dispatched straight through `reflection.call_agent`, whose boundary turns any replayed `$katari_ref` into
the `file` it denotes."
data tool_call(name: string, ref: call_ref, args: unknown)

@"A tool's output for the model, carrying the @ref@ of the call it answers so it round-trips as a function
response, and that call's tool @name@ so a wire that keys its responses by name has it to hand. @files@
are the `file` values found in the result: @text@ already shows their `$katari_ref` handles, and a
provider that can inline their content does so while the result is fresh."
data tool_result(name: string, ref: call_ref, text: string, files: array[file])

@"A conversation turn recording the model's tool-call batch — replayed so the next step shows the model what it already asked for."
data call_turn(calls: array[tool_call])

@"A conversation turn carrying the results of a tool-call batch."
data result_turn(results: array[tool_result])

// One conversation-history element. Each provider maps it to whatever its API calls content, so the
// function-calling loop closes. (Type synonyms take no docs.)
type message = turn | call_turn | result_turn

@"One inference step's decision: a final reply text for the user."
data step_final(text: string)

@"One inference step's decision: invoke a batch of tools (dispatched in parallel, results fed back together)."
data step_call(calls: array[tool_call])

// One inference step's decision. (Type synonyms take no docs.)
type step = step_final | step_call

@"One step's token accounting, as the provider's API reported it. @input_tokens@ counts the whole context
the step consumed, so the freshest step's figure is the session's current occupancy — figures across steps
do not add. @output_tokens@ counts what the model generated on the step."
data usage(input_tokens: integer, output_tokens: integer)

@"What a provider returns for one model step: the decision plus its token accounting."
data step_result(step: step, usage: usage)

@"What a provider returns for one structured-output step: the decoded object (the wire's best effort
at the requested schema — `ai.infer_structured` validates it as T) plus the step's token accounting."
data object_result(value: unknown, usage: usage)
